/-!
# Traps for 21 blocks of period 9: a wall of period nine and the background it enters

The block `001011111` of period 9 has a trap of 43 cells with labels modulo 9 (`trap001011111` of
[WordTraps](WordTraps.md)), the closure of the true window of a right half that it drives. Carried leftward through
the columns that the rule determines from it and from the trap's first cells at its white phases, it gives a trap of
`43 + d` cells, with the same 233 states and labels modulo 9, to the block of the column `d` places left; from distance
10 those columns repeat with spatial period 135, a background of period 9 in which every column repeats a block of
period 9. Here the 21 distinct blocks of period 9 among them, at distances 0 to 21, with their traps.

* `nineTraps`, `nineTraps_check`: the 21 traps, checked by the kernel at once.
* `nineTraps_blocks`: the blocks they are for.
* `nine_absorption_excludes`: entry into its trap, in the form of the kit's `AbsorptionT`, excludes each of the 21
  blocks as a tail of the center column.

The natural-language argument is `NineTraps.md`, beside this file.
-/

